 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** $O(N \cdot M)$ where $N$ is the number of pixels and $M$ is the number of samples per ray. The first pass is $O(1)$ relative to resolution (fixed cube rendering) [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** $O(N)$ for the two endpoint textures (2 floats per pixel) plus the volume texture [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Strengths:** Simple to implement; leverages standard GPU rasterization; avoids complex analytical intersection math in shaders [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Limitations:** Requires two rendering passes; requires additional memory for endpoint textures; less efficient than hierarchical traversal methods for large sparse volumes because it samples every voxel along the ray regardless of emptiness [S1, unofficial].
-*   **When to use:** Small to medium volumes; educational purposes; simple implementations where hierarchical structures are too complex [S1, unofficial].
-*   **When not to use:** Large sparse volumes (use [Sparse Voxel Traversal](link) or [Octree Traversal](link)); real-time applications requiring high performance on large datasets [S1, unofficial].
